# scripts/honeypot-names.txt.example
#
# Template for local/honeypot-names.txt — the private list of honeypot
# identifiers that the pre-commit hook + preflight gate 9 scan committed
# files against.
#
# Setup:
#   cp scripts/honeypot-names.txt.example local/honeypot-names.txt
#   $EDITOR local/honeypot-names.txt   # add your real identifiers, one per line
#   bash scripts/install-pre-commit-hook.sh
#
# The local/ directory is gitignored, so your real identifiers never reach
# committed code. The hook + preflight gate refuse any commit that contains
# a substring match (case-insensitive) on any name in the list.
#
# What to add: organization names, domain names, characteristic email
# locals — anything that uniquely identifies a honeypot you don't want
# linked to your project publicly.
#
# Lines starting with # are ignored. Blank lines are ignored.
#
# Examples (replace with your own):
# <YOUR_HONEYPOT_ORG_NAME_1>
# <YOUR_HONEYPOT_DOMAIN_1>
# <YOUR_HONEYPOT_ORG_NAME_2>
